__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Source reports and generated tables.
# These are large (well over 1 GB) and are not meant to live in git: they were
# briefly routed through Git LFS, which only moves the bytes into GitHub's
# metered LFS quota instead of removing them. Both sets are regenerable —
# Reports/ from the official sources listed in reports_185_1990/SOURCES.md,
# Out/ by re-running the pipeline scripts — so they are simply ignored.
#
# The extensions are listed in both cases: the pipeline writes the per-table
# PDFs as .PDF and the tables as .csv, while the source reports are .pdf.
# Git patterns are case-sensitive unless core.ignorecase is set, so a lowercase
# *.pdf alone would stop matching the generated files and leave Out/ untracked
# but visible. Out/ is also ignored wholesale as the authoritative rule.
Out/
*.pdf
*.PDF
*.csv
*.xls
# Per-year directories under reports_185_1990/, added for the PDFs above.
#
# *.pdf does NOT cover these: when a worktree has no PDFs of its own, the years
# are often symlinked in from another checkout rather than re-downloaded. Git
# sees a directory entry named "2024", not a *.pdf, so it offers to commit the
# symlink -- and the symlink points at an absolute path outside the repo, so it
# is dead for everyone else.
#
# No trailing slash, and that is the whole point. A trailing slash restricts the
# pattern to directories, and git treats a symlink as a file, so "*/" ignores a
# real year directory and still offers the symlink -- the one commit the comment
# above exists to prevent. "20*" matches both, and still tracks manifest.tsv.
reports_185_1990/20*
*.XLS
*.xlsx
*.XLSX
